@startuml
title Guarded routing: one route group under first-match and all-match
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "firstMatch group\n(unique priorities required)" as FM #E9F5EA {
  state "Source node\n(disposition matched the group trigger)" as FMSrc #DCEEFF
  state choiceFM <<choice>>
  FMSrc --> choiceFM : evaluate guards in\n<latex>(p(e), \mathrm{id}(e))</latex> order
  state "Target A (priority 0)" as FMA #D9EFDF
  state "Target B (priority 1)" as FMB #DCEEFF
  state "noMatch policy" as FMNo #FFE0C8
  choiceFM --> FMA : first true guard\n(exactly one fires)
  choiceFM --> FMB : only if A's guard was false
  choiceFM --> FMNo : no guard true /\ncomplete: output + scope result\nskip: consume silently\nfail: hard error
}

state "allMatches group" as AM #DCEEFF {
  state "Source node " as AMSrc #DCEEFF
  state forkAM <<fork>>
  AMSrc --> forkAM : evaluate ALL guards
  state "Target X" as AMX #D9EFDF
  state "Target Y" as AMY #D9EFDF
  state "Target Z" as AMZ #D9EFDF
  forkAM --> AMX : guard true
  forkAM --> AMY : guard true
  forkAM --> AMZ : guard false: no token
  note on link
    every true guard emits one child token;
    more than one emission mints a fork epoch
    <latex>\varepsilon' = H(\mathit{run} \Vert \varepsilon_{\mathrm{top}} \Vert \mathit{group} \Vert \mathit{gen})</latex>
  end note
}

note bottom of FM #EAF7EE
Trigger filtering precedes guard evaluation: a failed
activity can never traverse a completed route merely
because its predicate is true. Groups of one disposition
all fire in the same Route microstep, each with its own
selection; an unobserved Rholang guard anywhere among
them blocks the whole token until its observation lands.
end note
@enduml
